This week Paris des Arts decamps to Geneva, the cosmopolitan Swiss city nestled between the lake and the Jura mountains. Valérie Fayolle is there to meet two artists who have made it their home. Young chef Danny Khezzar heads up the team at the Michelin-starred Bayview restaurant. A "Top Chef" finalist in 2014, Khezzar has two passions: music and cooking.    
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcf6305e-b8c1-11f1-9034-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ASSEMBLAGE-PDA-SPE-GENEVE-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcf6305e-b8c1-11f1-9034-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ASSEMBLAGE-PDA-SPE-GENEVE-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69d54cf6-b8c2-11f1-950b-c5840a5359ca</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:18:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie FAYOLLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Each side feels it 'could get a decisive military victory' in Sudan, Trump's Africa envoy says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-each-side-feels-it-could-get-a-decisive-military-victory-in-sudan-trump-s-africa-envoy-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Trump's Africa envoy Massad Boulos said that each side in Sudan feels it "could get a decisive military victory". Asked about Western Sahara, he acknowledged there is no "imminent solution that we can feel or touch". He also rejected Rwanda's accusations of bias over US sanctions, saying they "can easily be reversed".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/797a3062-b8cd-11f1-9fbe-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/FRproduction2-2026-09-24-11-25-50.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/797a3062-b8cd-11f1-9fbe-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/FRproduction2-2026-09-24-11-25-50.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f04bea3a-b7fd-11f1-a5ca-15e75cf33873</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:54:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>War, AI, secularism, surrogacy: what to take away from the Pope's speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/war-ai-secularism-surrogacy-what-to-take-away-from-the-pope-s-speech</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV used his address at the Élysée Palace to touch on some of France's biggest debates, from artificial intelligence and secularism to surrogacy, while calling for peace and solidarity. Our journalist Kethevane Gorjestani breaks down the key takeaways from his speech.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06f111d4-b8d0-11f1-95b7-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T104733Z-954048956-RC2AQNA1FRKQ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06f111d4-b8d0-11f1-95b7-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T104733Z-954048956-RC2AQNA1FRKQ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">053a148e-b8d6-11f1-bd52-399e471fc178</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:27:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump made ‘final decision’ to allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says</link><description>
President Donald Trump told President Volodymyr Zelensky that he had made a "final decision" to grant Kyiv the licence to produce Patriot air defence missiles, the Ukrainian leader said Friday. The assurance came during the last meeting between the two leaders, Zelensky said, capping a period of uncertainty after a series of reversals on the issue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16058bd4-b8c4-11f1-86f7-110fe1281c4e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:46:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dae10fc-b8c3-11f1-92c1-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266056109006.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Canadian-Haitian writer Thélyson Orélien stripped from Prix Goncourt longlist after AI claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260925-canadian-haitian-writer-th%C3%A9lyson-or%C3%A9lien-stripped-from-prix-goncourt-longlist-after-ai-claims</link><description>
Canadian-Haitian novelist Thélyson Orélien was removed from the Prix Goncourt literary prize longlist following online claims that the book was largely written by artificial intelligence (AI), the organisers of France's top literary prize said Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a7fd0fc-b8a3-11f1-b221-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/bce6ebde6a47428c69bdfe67091fff522ef2d1ac.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a7fd0fc-b8a3-11f1-b221-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/bce6ebde6a47428c69bdfe67091fff522ef2d1ac.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f4dedae-b8d3-11f1-8884-fbddf4fc8b33</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:35:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a7fd0fc-b8a3-11f1-b221-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/bce6ebde6a47428c69bdfe67091fff522ef2d1ac.jpg">© Joël Saget, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Fatalities on Indian roads: One death reported every three minutes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes</link><description>
India has the second-largest road network in the world, spanning over 6 million kilometres. But these roads are silent killers, with one death reported every three minutes. Every day, headlines are filled with horror stories: drunk drivers mowing people down, school buses hit by speeding trucks killing children, buses with dozens of passengers plunging into gorges.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd861ccc-b82a-11f1-ab73-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-INDIA-ROAD-SAFETY-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd861ccc-b82a-11f1-ab73-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-INDIA-ROAD-SAFETY-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c6ae98c-b82b-11f1-8dd9-1bd6ea2dfd4d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:33:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Navodita KUMARI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>From 'Jungle' to jungles, migrants in Calais continue to dream of UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk</link><description>
October 2026 marks 10 years since the Calais "Jungle" in northern France was dismantled by French police. The camp was home to thousands of migrants who wanted to cross the Channel and reach the UK. A decade on, migrants continue to dream of reaching British shores and the "Jungle" has been replaced by many smaller jungles scattered along the northern French coastline. FRANCE 24's Pauline Godart, Claire Paccalin and Mohamed Farhat report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4033b46e-b813-11f1-a6d5-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-calais-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4033b46e-b813-11f1-a6d5-41bcac5946c5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-calais-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bed0d594-b828-11f1-ac0c-11ee5c0bceef</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:30:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pauline GODART</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY : Pope Leo XIV's speech from the Élysée</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-replay-pope-leo-xiv-s-speech-from-the-%C3%A9lys%C3%A9e</link><description>
Watch the replay of Pope Leo XIV's address in french at the Élysée Palace on 25 September, where he spoke about peace, artificial intelligence, France's challenges and the importance of solidarity. The pontiff also condemned gestational surrogacy, calling for greater protection of human dignity during the first day of his four-day visit to France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88adc896-b8d2-11f1-9c15-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T110455Z-872970339-RC2BQNAHNB8P-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88adc896-b8d2-11f1-9c15-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T110455Z-872970339-RC2BQNAHNB8P-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02f70b4a-b8d2-11f1-bc90-4957554054e9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:26:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Deadly Russian drone strike hits central Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-ukraine-deadly-russian-drone-strike-hits-central-kyiv</link><description>
A Russian drone strike hit central Kyiv before 8am on 25 September, killing a 14-year-old and leaving rescue workers clearing rubble from damaged buildings. Residents said there was little time to react to the air raid sirens, as Russia's increasingly deadly drone attacks also struck logistics facilities and postal infrastructure elsewhere in the city. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg has the details from Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1b2bf4a-ae12-11f1-afdf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-11T171619Z-133128444-RC24HNA5JZM9-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1b2bf4a-ae12-11f1-afdf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-11T171619Z-133128444-RC24HNA5JZM9-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e5f46f42-b8d1-11f1-ad35-9304979ecc94</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:24:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia: what's driving the renewed violence in Tigray?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-what-s-driving-the-renewed-violence-in-tigray</link><description>
Tigray's rebel authorities say they are now in a "full-blown war" with the Ethiopian government, as fighting spreads into the neighbouring Amhara and Afar regions. Ethiopia's federal army says 272 rebels were killed and 260 wounded in the north, while FRANCE 24 spoke to Jervin Naidoo, Political Analyst at Oxford Economics Africa, to assess the seriousness of the escalation and explain what is driving the renewed violence in northern Ethiopia
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/571bf428-b8ce-11f1-b587-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-214628-215253-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/571bf428-b8ce-11f1-b587-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-214628-215253-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5c437c5a-b8ce-11f1-987d-bb56e7b88af6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:15:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal: power cuts return as Dakar swelters in the heat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-power-cuts-return-as-dakar-swelters-in-the-heat</link><description>
After years of largely stabilising its electricity supply, Senegal is once again facing power cuts, with outages returning to Dakar in September. The blackouts are fuelling frustration among residents as the capital endures a spell of intense heat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62253884-b8ce-11f1-9d75-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-215340-215529-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62253884-b8ce-11f1-9d75-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-215340-215529-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">672699ae-b8ce-11f1-a6e0-6d0a33389317</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:14:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia: Tigray rebels claim "full-blown war"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tigray-rebels-claim-full-blown-war</link><description>
The Tigray People's Liberation Front says it is in a "full-blown war" with Ethiopia's federal government after seizing key airports and launching attacks into the neighbouring Amhara and Afar regions. The escalation comes days after the TPLF joined six other armed groups in a new alliance against the government, raising fears of a return to the devastating 2020-2022 conflict that killed at least 600,000 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b87fdf8-8fe1-11f1-8fcf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26053289258521.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b87fdf8-8fe1-11f1-8fcf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26053289258521.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a3f5524-b8cd-11f1-a9c4-efa76f09ebdc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:13:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia: renewed Tigray fighting raises fears of return to civil war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-renewed-tigray-fighting-raises-fears-of-return-to-civil-war</link><description>
Fears are mounting that Ethiopia could be sliding back towards civil war as fighting intensifies in the north, with the army saying it killed 272 TPLF fighters in Amhara while the rebels describe the conflict as a "full-blown war." The escalation comes after the TPLF joined a new alliance with six other armed groups. FRANCE 24's Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4b4ab32-b81c-11f1-9a75-9d4ae5c4ba17/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T101012Z-919341318-RC2KPNA74E5F-RTRMADP-3-ETHIOPIA-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4b4ab32-b81c-11f1-9a75-9d4ae5c4ba17/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T101012Z-919341318-RC2KPNA74E5F-RTRMADP-3-ETHIOPIA-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">abc79efc-b8cc-11f1-ae57-058f3134f086</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:12:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Pope Leo XIV begins Paris diplomacy at the Élysée</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-france-pope-leo-xiv-begins-paris-diplomacy-at-the-%C3%A9lys%C3%A9e</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV has arrived in Paris, and was welcomed at the Élysée Palace by French president Emmanuel Macron. They are having closed-door talks on international geopolitics, artificial intelligence and peace. The pontiff is then set to deliver a speech at the Élysée Palace. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd1092b4-b8ca-11f1-af8d-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-120047-120539-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd1092b4-b8ca-11f1-af8d-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-120047-120539-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d204736c-b8ca-11f1-ad5b-cdbd4154f78c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:10:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Pope Leo gives first address of France visit at Élysée presidential palace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">f25d52a0-b8ca-11f1-9c2b-bd02fb586fde</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:22:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Journalism and resistance under Taliban rule</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule</link><description>
In this edition, we focus on Afghanistan, which recently marked the fifth anniversary of the Taliban's return to power. Since then, the exclusion of women and girls has become normalised, with the government systematically dismantling the rights of more than half the country's population.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f937a684-b8c5-11f1-9764-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/vanishing-girl-kabul-web-photo.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f937a684-b8c5-11f1-9764-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/vanishing-girl-kabul-web-photo.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65703b5e-b8c6-11f1-94d9-1d5ad55c08cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:21:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Top European leagues demand FIFA reforms, piling pressure on Infantino</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260925-english-spanish-italian-german-football-leagues-call-for-fifa-reform</link><description>
FIFA president Gianni Infantino came under increased pressure Friday as Europe's four main football leagues called for sweeping reforms of the world football governing body. The English Premier League, Spain's La Liga, Italy's Serie A and Germany's Bundesliga demanded that measures are adopted to ensure "disciplinary matters remain demonstrably insulated from political interference".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/900f9906-b8c9-11f1-8125-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/1aa70042f5889e6cca4e17b7846ced00bddb631c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/900f9906-b8c9-11f1-8125-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/1aa70042f5889e6cca4e17b7846ced00bddb631c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">91688e20-b8c9-11f1-8f43-0b2a107b10ed</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:12:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/900f9906-b8c9-11f1-8125-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/1aa70042f5889e6cca4e17b7846ced00bddb631c.jpg">© Fabrice Coffrini, AFP (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>US rapper Macklemore announces 'Free Palestine' tour after Ed Sheeran saga</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260925-us-rapper-macklemore-announces-free-palestine-tour-after-ed-sheeran-sa</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Friday, September 25: There's anticipation and excitement in France as Pope Leo XIV embarks on the first papal visit to France in 18 years. It comes at a time of renewed Catholic faith among young French people. Also, we look at reactions after Italy's new legislation banning full-face Islamic headwear from schools. Plus: US rapper Macklemore announces a new "Free Palestine" tour that will raise funds for humanitarian groups.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1fbd7f50-b8b1-11f1-b7bf-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-25T06-44-13-754Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1fbd7f50-b8b1-11f1-b7bf-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-25T06-44-13-754Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b5e85e12-b8a4-11f1-a4e0-25e798ff330b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:54:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo visits France: Pontiff wants to focus world's attention on peace, human dignity, technology</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-visits-france-pontiff-wants-to-focus-world-s-attention-on-peace-human-dignity-technology</link><description>
Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Andrea Antonio Verardi, Professor of Church History and Cultural Heritage at the Pontifical Gregorian University. According to Verardi, Pope Leo’s visit to France is much more than a diplomatic visit. The focus of the visit combines three key issues: the search for peace amid geopolitical instability, the challenge that artificial intelligence and technological change pose to humanity and human dignity, and the unexpected re-emergence of religious identification among younger generations in a deeply secular society.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de2ccdc8-b8c1-11f1-b6c7-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-080110-081455-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de2ccdc8-b8c1-11f1-b6c7-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-080110-081455-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3dc26f6-b8c1-11f1-b9dd-27a9ce888343</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:50:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Pope Leo XIV welcomed by Macron at the Élysée</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-france-pope-leo-xiv-welcomed-by-macron-at-the-%C3%A9lys%C3%A9e</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron welcomed Pope Leo XIV to the Élysée Palace on Friday, 25 September, at the start of the pontiff's four-day visit to France. The Pope entered the courtyard to a ceremonial welcome, walked the red carpet, shook hands with President Macron and First Lady Brigitte Macron, before climbing the palace steps for a brief meeting at the Élysée.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b29abc2-b8c4-11f1-9d63-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-111621-112214-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b29abc2-b8c4-11f1-9d63-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-111621-112214-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70113ed4-b8c4-11f1-a659-df246c1eb60c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:48:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump courts Xi Jinping during high-profile White House visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit</link><description>
President Donald Trump rolled out an unusually lavish welcome for Chinese President Xi Jinping, praising their personal friendship throughout a White House state dinner and other ceremonial events. While both leaders said they held frank discussions behind closed doors, the visit produced no major breakthroughs, prompting criticism from Democratic lawmakers who argued the pageantry overshadowed pressing issues including Iran, Taiwan, AI and trade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf9d2e2-b8c2-11f1-bed0-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-081530-081716-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf9d2e2-b8c2-11f1-bed0-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-081530-081716-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3a3f2ea-b8c2-11f1-820b-4516fe4dabea</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:38:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY : Pope Leo XIV arrives in France for four-day visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-pope-leo-xiv-arrives-in-france-for-four-day-visit</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV has landed at Paris Orly Airport for the start of his four-day visit to France. A welcoming ceremony was held on the tarmac in the presence of President Emmanuel Macron, marking the beginning of a programme combining diplomatic meetings with major public events across Paris, Lourdes and Metz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2e8022c-b8bb-11f1-a878-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T082052Z-2003509193-RC28QNAR7QZT-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2e8022c-b8bb-11f1-a878-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T082052Z-2003509193-RC28QNAR7QZT-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2c7c34cc-b8be-11f1-a69b-818a13dd31b6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:01:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's Catholic influencers take faith from social media to real life</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-catholic-influencers-take-faith-from-social-media-to-real-life</link><description>
Catholic influencers gathered hundreds of young people for an evening of prayer at Paris's Saint-Sulpice church ahead of Pope Leo XIV's visit, highlighting how social media is becoming a new tool for evangelisation. As youth baptisms rise in France, creators say their goal is to turn online engagement into real-life communities, while Church leaders warn that influencers themselves should not overshadow the faith they promote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a309ce68-b8bb-11f1-9290-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-080757-080940-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a309ce68-b8bb-11f1-9290-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-080757-080940-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9084cae-b8bb-11f1-89a4-0f42465b335a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:53:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
